*Heading
Simply supported [0/90/0] square plate, SC8R composite, sinusoidal pressure (quarter model)
** a = 1, plate 0 <= x, y <= a, this quarter 0 <= x, y <= a/2 with symmetry on x = y = a/2; q = sin(pi x) sin(pi y),
** one value per element (its centre). validate_with_ccx.py runs a/h = 100 and a/h = 10 and compares the centre
** deflection with classical laminate theory (Navier) and Pagano's 3-D elasticity solution.
** One layer of SC8R continuum shells (z = -h/2 to h/2), relative ply thicknesses. ccx has no layered solid
** section: abq2ccx writes one C3D8I per ply, with the ply interface nodes on the stack edges.
*Parameter
h = 0.01
zb = -h / 2.
zt = h / 2.
